@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif
skinparam roundCorner 8

title Pointer-Screen Cascade & Active Screen Elimination Flow

actor User as u
participant "macOS Cursor\n(NSEvent mouseLocation)" as mouse
participant "Global Hotkey\n(Opt+Cmd+C)" as hotkey
participant "CascadeBarApp\n(main_bar.m)" as bar
participant "ScreenManager" as sm
collections "Connected Monitors\n(C49RG9x & Retina)" as screens
collections "Active Windows" as wins

== 1. Pointer-Driven Shortkey Invocation ==
u -> mouse : Move cursor to desired monitor (e.g. Display 1)
u -> hotkey : Press Option + Command + C
hotkey -> bar : HotKeyHandler -> performCascade:
bar -> sm : +screenForPointer
sm -> mouse : [NSEvent mouseLocation]
mouse --> sm : Cocoa Point (x, y)
sm -> screens : Match point against screen.cocoaFrame
screens --> sm : Display 1 (Pointer Screen)
sm --> bar : return Display 1

== 2. Isolated Monitor Cascade Execution ==
bar -> wins : Filter windows located on Display 1
bar -> bar : Calculate invariant cascade frames on Display 1
bar -> wins : Apply target frames & restack Z on Display 1 only
note right of wins
  Windows on Display 0 remain 100% untouched!
  Zero focus-click required to switch target display.
end note

== 3. Simplified Menu Structure ==
note over bar
  "Active Screen (Follows Focus)" REMOVED:
  - Eliminates fragile key-window tracking
  - Shortkey intuitively cascades pointer screen
  - "Cascade All Screens" available for full arrangement
  - Target Screen submenu dedicates solely to Auto-Rearrange
end note
@enduml
